 "standard_text": "Integrate xⁿ (including n = −1), eᵏˣ, sin kx, cos kx and related sums; integration by substitution and by parts; integrate using partial fractions; evaluate the area between two curves.",
 "meta_desc": "Free Year 13 A level maths worksheets on integration techniques: standard integrals, ln and eˣ, substitution, integration by parts, partial fractions and definite integrals. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "∫ 1/x dx = ln|x| + c; ∫ eᵏˣ dx = (1/k)eᵏˣ + c.",
 "key_sub": "Parts: ∫ u (dv/dx) dx = uv − ∫ v (du/dx) dx.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How it works</h2><p>Standard integrals: ∫ 1/<i>x</i> d<i>x</i> = ln|<i>x</i>| + <i>c</i>, ∫ e<sup><i>kx</i></sup> d<i>x</i> = (1/<i>k</i>)e<sup><i>kx</i></sup> + <i>c</i>, ∫ cos <i>kx</i> d<i>x</i> = (1/<i>k</i>) sin <i>kx</i> + <i>c</i>.</p><p>Substitution: replace an inner function by <i>u</i> and d<i>x</i> by d<i>u</i>/(d<i>u</i>/d<i>x</i>). By parts: choose <i>u</i> to become simpler when differentiated. Split rational functions into partial fractions before integrating.</p><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>∫ <i>x</i>e<sup><i>x</i></sup> d<i>x</i></p><p class='sn-ex-s'><i>u</i> = <i>x</i>, d<i>v</i>/d<i>x</i> = e<sup><i>x</i></sup></p><p class='sn-ex-s'><i>x</i>e<sup><i>x</i></sup> − ∫ e<sup><i>x</i></sup> d<i>x</i></p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: e<sup><i>x</i></sup>(<i>x</i> − 1) + <i>c</i></p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Forgetting to divide by k.</li><li>Choosing u = eˣ in integration by parts.</li><li>Forgetting the modulus in ln|x|.</li></ul>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "When do you use integration by parts?",
   "a": "When the integrand is a product, such as x eˣ or x sin x. Choose u to be the part that gets simpler when differentiated."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do you integrate 1/(ax + b)?",
   "a": "∫ 1/(ax + b) dx = (1/a) ln|ax + b| + c."
  }
 ],
